{"id":352,"slug":"haxan","title":"Häxan","year":1922,"country":"Denmark","duration":105,"spine":134,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/352-haxan","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/release_boxshots/4875-a31914ec658fcdad321e78e4356e6349/7o7Guh861KsyRUBCmBrGvlrRmyg6gB_original.jpg","description":"\nGrave robbing, torture, possessed nuns, and a satanic Sabbath: Benjamin Christensen’s legendary silent film uses a series of dramatic vignettes to explore the scientific hypothesis that the witches of the Middle Ages and early modern era suffered from the same ills as psychiatric patients diagnosed with hysteria in the film's own time. Far from a dry dissertation on the topic, the film itself is a witches’ brew of the scary, the gross, and the darkly humorous. Christensen’s mix-and-match approach to genre anticipates gothic horror, documentary re-creation, and the essay film, making for an experience unlike anything else in the history of cinema.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Benjamin Christensen","slug":"benjamin-christensen"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Benjamin Christensen","role":"The devil","slug":"benjamin-christensen"},{"actor":"Astrid Holm","role":"The printer’s wife, Anna","slug":"astrid-holm"},{"actor":"Karen Winther","role":"Anna’s sister","slug":"karen-winther"},{"actor":"Maren Pedersen","role":"Maria the weaver, a witch","slug":"maren-pedersen"},{"actor":"Wilhelmine Henriksen","role":"Apelone, a poor old woman","slug":"wilhelmine-henriksen"},{"actor":"Kate Fabian","role":"Old maid","slug":"kate-fabian"},{"actor":"Oscar Stribolt","role":"Friar","slug":"oscar-stribolt"},{"actor":"Clara Pontoppidan","role":"Sister Cecilia","slug":"clara-pontoppidan"},{"actor":"Alice O’Fredericks","role":"Nun","slug":"alice-ofredericks"},{"actor":"Johannes Andersen","role":"Father Henrik, witch judge","slug":"johannes-andersen"},{"actor":"Elith Pio","role":"Johannes, witch judge","slug":"elith-pio"},{"actor":"Aage Hertel","role":"Witch judge","slug":"